  "revision": {
   "cross_federation_design": "one model per configuration, trained on the honest innovations of every client in rounds 12-35 of CAL seeds 0 and 1, scored on every seed; headline over the other seeds",
   "why_invalid": "each seed is an independently trained federation (own initialisation, own client models), so prototype spaces share no coordinates and a density model of one federation's raw innovations does not transfer to another. Honest rows only, rounds 12-35, seeds 0-2: the top 10 principal components fitted on one seed explain 0.018-0.066 of another seed's variance (CIFAR-100 0.5 and CIFAR-10), against 0.72-0.74 for odd rounds of the same seed fitted on its even rounds; cosines between seeds' mean innovations are -0.021 to 0.035; on the held-out honest rows, predicting zero (0.995 / 0.939 / 0.972 per entry) beats predicting the CAL mean (1.051 / 1.017 / 1.036). The low held-out reconstruction quality was first attributed to memorisation; it is the absence of shared coordinates.",
   "inspected": "the attacked AUCs of both runs had been computed and read before the within-federation design was fixed; that design was fixed on honest data only (rows of the seed's own rounds 2-11 and 12-35) before any attacked payload was scored with it; afterwards a code-path smoke test with 8 Adam steps (CIFAR-10) printed AUCs of an essentially untrained model, which were not used for anything",
